data.content:
**Summary:** In MSTest v4, the `TestMethodAttribute(string displayName)` constructor was removed. Instead, set the `DisplayName` property:

```csharp
// Before (MSTest v3):
public MyAttribute(string name) : base(name) { }

// After (MSTest v4):
public MyAttribute(string name) { DisplayName = name; }
```

Your current code doesn't call `base(category)`, so it should compile fine as-is. If you have a version that was calling `base(displayName)`, just remove that base call and assign `DisplayName = displayName;` in the constructor body.
